invariant: INV-14
file: src/x509_end_point.c
catches: scram_test
reason: ch_tls_server_end_point hashes a sha384WithRSAEncryption
  certificate with SHA-256. RFC 5929 section 4.1 takes the hash of the
  certificate's signature algorithm, and SHA-256 only in place of MD5 and
  SHA-1. The value is then 32 bytes that no peer computes, so
  SCRAM-SHA-256-PLUS fails against every server whose certificate a
  SHA-384 signature covers, and the call still returns CH_OK.
  bin/scram_test holds the value to hashlib's for a certificate OpenSSL
  signed with each algorithm.

--- old
    ROW(sha256_with_rsa, SHA256_LEN), ROW(sha384_with_rsa, SHA384_LEN),
--- new
    ROW(sha256_with_rsa, SHA256_LEN), ROW(sha384_with_rsa, SHA256_LEN),
